  "description": "Instructional sine/cosine reduction table: four source columns, blank numbering header, seven aligned data entries inside the original 3-1-3 ruled grouping. Clean spacing, line weights and coordinates are unmeasured modern typesetting regularization, not numerical source data. The original angle glyph is a/alpha-shaped and alphabetically unresolved in the pixel inventory; Greek alpha is bound to the approved official context, not claimed to be independently decoded from pixels. No additional values, conditions, answers or captions.",
